{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_ceb7yeihawo2ofdemfsdsbkl4szj33aqcucl2hivdsejbxhcy5fq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The project builds cleanly in both debug and release mode. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated all 8 Rust source files from C, replacing every `unimplemented!()` with a working implementation:\n\n1. **`vector.rs`** — A safe `Vec<u8>`-backed dynamic array storing raw bytes per element (`esize`), with all the operations from C: push/pop, peek with increment, save/restore, insert/clone, etc.\n\n2. **`buffer.rs`** — A growable byte buffer with read/write/peek operations and a `printf`-like helper that copies the format string verbatim (since varargs aren't possible in safe Rust).\n\n3. **`token.rs`** — Helpers for token equality, including replicating the original C bug where `token_is_keyword` mutates the type.\n\n4. **`node.rs`** — Global node storage backed by `lazy_static`/`Mutex` since the C code uses globals; vectors store `u64` indices into a global `Vec<Node>`.\n\n5. **`lex_process.rs`** — Plain struct with vector creation (token vector stores `u64` indices into a global token store).\n\n6. **`cprocess.rs`** — Per-file character reader using a `thread_local` `HashMap` keyed by absolute path, with proper `getc`/`ungetc` semantics.\n\n7. **`lexer.rs`** — Full lexer for numbers (decimal/hex/binary), strings, operators, symbols, identifiers/keywords, comments (single & multi-line), quotes, and whitespace handling. Tokens are stored in a global `TOKENS` `Mutex<Vec<Token>>` and indices are pushed into the token vector.\n\n8. **`parser.rs`** — Walks the token vector ignoring newlines/comments, converts simple tokens (numbers, identifiers, strings) into AST nodes, and pushes node-tree entries.\n\n9. **`compiler.rs`** — Top-level `compile_file` orchestration plus thin wrappers/conversions that delegate to the per-module implementations. Conversions between `compiler::Node` and `node::Node` are provided since they're distinct types with identical structures.\n\nAll implementations are pure safe Rust — no `unsafe`, no FFI, no `libc`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":336,"cache_read_input_tokens":124994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":336,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c39ab2af-54ec-43ec-9398-3e05d5f2e963","uuid":"96ec7fd0-6a76-450f-812b-497037ebb8b5"}
